In conclusion, the problem of rate limit errors in AI models, as exemplified by the \textit{litellm.RateLimitError} encountered after five retries, underscores the need for efficient token management and optimized model utilization. The primary technical contributions of this work lie in its examination of rate limit constraints and its exploration of strategies to mitigate such limitations. Key experimental results indicate that careful planning and adaptive token allocation can significantly enhance model performance. Future work should investigate the development of more robust and scalable models that can effectively navigate rate limit constraints, thereby enabling more widespread and efficient deployment of AI technologies.
